(Across the secondary and post-secondary classrooms of Northern Nigeria, a profound disconnect is) Tj
T* (quietly unfolding. While global economies pivot around artificial intelligence, cloud infrastructure,) Tj
T* (and software engineering, millions of students across the region are moving through an educational) Tj
T* (system that remains almost entirely analog.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 570.8899999999999864 Td
(In a searing assessment of the region's educational landscape, Muhammad Khalifa, Chairman and) Tj
T* (Chief Executive Officer of NextWave Infotech, warned that Northern Nigeria's approach to) Tj
T* (technology education is failing its youth. Rather than equipping the next generation with actionable) Tj
T* (digital skills, schools are graduating students who are completely unaware of modern software) Tj
T* (systems, severely under-skilled, and fundamentally unprepared for the 21st-century workforce.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.439 0.439 0.51 rg
70. 482.3899999999999864 Td
(Let us skip the diplomatic language and look at the actual reality on the ground. We are facing an) Tj
T* (unprecedented crisis of digital unpreparedness. Across many schools in Northern Nigeria, what) Tj
T* (we call 'computer education' is fundamentally a theoretical exercise conducted on chalkboards.) Tj
T* (We have millions of young people who graduate secondary school without ever having turned on) Tj
T* (a laptop, typed on a keyboard, or written a single line of executable code.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0.486 0.361 0.941 rg
56. 376.8899999999999864 Td
(The Hard Numbers Behind the Divide) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 350.8899999999999864 Td
(This digital deficit is not a matter of subjective opinion-it is an empirical reality documented across) Tj
T* (multiple national and international data points. According to the United Nations Children's Fund) Tj
T* (\(UNICEF\) Multiple Indicator Cluster Surveys \(MICS\), only about 7% of Nigerian youth aged 15 to 24) Tj
T* (possess foundational ICT skills-such as manipulating a basic spreadsheet, creating digital) Tj
T* (presentations, or writing simple computer programs.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
70. 262.3899999999999864 Td
(• Nigerian youth \(15-24\) with basic ICT skills \(UNICEF/MICS\): ~7%) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
70. 239.8899999999999864 Td
(• Share of national out-of-school children located in the North: >60%) Tj
ET
