(The Anatomy of a Systemic Failure) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 715.8899999999999864 Td
(According to the NextWave Infotech CEO, the failure of technological education across northern) Tj
T* (schools stems from three interconnected structural breakdowns:) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 669.8899999999999864 Td
(1. The Illusion of "Computer Studies") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 644.8899999999999864 Td
(In most public secondary institutions, technology education exists strictly on paper. Students write) Tj
T* (examinations testing their ability to memorize hardware definitions or draw computer components) Tj
T* (on paper without ever interacting with a physical machine.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 589.3899999999999864 Td
(At NextWave Infotech, when we evaluate candidates for technical roles-even those holding) Tj
T* (university degrees in Computer Science-we regularly encounter graduates who cannot perform) Tj
T* (standard technical tasks. They can write down the definition of an algorithm because that is how) Tj
T* (they were evaluated. But place them in front of a development environment, ask them to query a) Tj
T* (database, or set up a local network, and they are completely stranded.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
70. 500.8899999999999864 Td
(• Traditional classroom model: theoretical definitions, rote memorization of hardware,) Tj
T* (paper-and-pencil exams.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
70. 461.8899999999999864 Td
(• Real-world tech demand: practical software engineering, cloud and database administration,) Tj
T* (hands-on problem solving.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
70. 422.8899999999999864 Td
(• The gap between the two: a generation trained to describe technology rather than to build with) Tj
T* (it.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 372.8899999999999864 Td
(2. Acute Infrastructure Collapse) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 347.8899999999999864 Td
(Practical digital education requires consistent power and internet connectivity-two resources in) Tj
T* (severe short supply across the region. Over 80% of rural and suburban public schools in Northern) Tj
T* (Nigeria lack reliable access to the electrical grid. Where computer laboratories exist on paper, they) Tj
T* (frequently sit locked, filled with obsolete, dust-covered hardware that lacks the power supply) Tj
T* (needed to run.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 252.3899999999999864 Td
(3. Educator Capability Deficit) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 227.3899999999999864 Td
(A major barrier to reform lies within the teaching corps itself. Most educators assigned to teach) Tj
T* (computer studies in primary and secondary schools suffer from severe digital illiteracy themselves.) Tj
T* (Relying on outdated syllabi from two decades ago, teachers lack access to continuous technical) Tj
T* (training, leaving them unable to impart modern technical competencies to their students.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0.486 0.361 0.941 rg
56. 142.3899999999999864 Td
(The Socio-Economic Cost of Inaction) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.11 0.11 0.149 rg
56. 116.3899999999999864 Td
(The long-term ramifications of this educational vacuum extend far beyond individual career) Tj
T* (prospects; they threaten the stability of the broader regional economy.) Tj
ET
